<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aliya Rama Raya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1565">1565</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aliya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> Raya was a nobleman of the Aravidu family and son-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a> who dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> as regent for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadashiva-raya">Sadashiva Raya</a> from the 1540s. He played the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a> against one another, but his interventions eventually united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar">Ahmadnagar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golconda-fort">Golconda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a> against him. He was captured and beheaded at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talikota">Battle of Talikota</a> in January 1565.</p></div>
